# CONTENT IS BYTE-IDENTICAL ON EVERY PLATFORM, OR EVERY NUMBER TAKEN FROM IT LIES.
#
# Found on Windows CI 2026-09-22: `CookedRegistryGate` reported that four shaders were "recorded at
# 2262 bytes and is 2327 tracked by this repository". Nothing had edited them. Git was checking them
# out with CRLF, so each file was larger on disk by exactly its line count — and the committed
# registry, which records a SIZE per entry, can never agree with both platforms at once.
#
# The registry is only where it surfaced. The same translation moves every content hash, every pak
# CRC and every `.dpak` a Windows machine packs, so an archive built there would not match one built
# here from the same commit. Marking content `-text` tells git to store and check it out verbatim:
# these files are DATA that happens to be readable, not source anybody diffs line by line.
#
# Deliberately NOT `* text=auto eol=lf`: that would rewrite line endings across the whole tree
# including C++ sources, which is a much larger change than the defect requires and would touch the
# working copy of everyone who has one.

# Shaders — hashed by the shader cache and recorded in the cooked registry.
*.shader   -text
*.glsl     -text
*.glslh    -text
*.vert     -text
*.frag     -text
*.comp     -text

# Authored content the registry sizes and the packager hashes.
*.desce        -text
*.demat        -text
*.deprefab     -text
*.anim         -text
*.skeleton     -text
*.stmesh       -text
*.skmesh       -text
*.derig        -text
*.danimgraph   -text
*.retarget     -text
*.decloudtype  -text
*.dclayout     -text
*.dcnv         -text
*.dcmv         -text
*.detheme      -text
*.destrings    -text
*.deproj       -text

# The cooked registry itself: its own sizes are compared against the files above.
*.dreg     -text
